out.append("- Modern line pass (Jes tg 17804, 17806, 17813, 17815): the show-all switch and the sticky gloss bar are gone; a modern line is always under the glossed sections, with 40 more plain respellings of ours (marked `lineOnly`, no popover) and the minimal-translation departures tabled above. New subtitle `Bred and mylk for childeren` (decided). Figures now sit inline at the start of their text; the Prologue's five part windows are new.")
out.append("- Contents redesign: the all-sections constellation chart at the top is gone; the top contents list only the major divisions, and each part heading carries a line of star links. Dropped `The Conclusiouns, as a constellacioun` (it named only Part II and no longer fits a list of all the parts). New: the Prologue's subtitle `Litell Lowis my sone`, the star lines' nav labels, the full-rubric star names.")
out.append("- Gloss review: Skeat's notes and introduction are no longer shown as definitions; labelled `Skeat's note` / `From Skeat's introduction` and set as notes (9 entries). Source name `Skeat's notes, Oxford Chaucer 1894` → `Skeat, Oxford Chaucer 1894, vol. III`.")
out.append("- Gloss variant (`treatise/style-gloss`): the Middle English / Both / Modern toggle and the column tags (`Chaucer`, `In modern English`) and `Modern rendering — pending` are gone. New: the gloss bar, popover labels, source names, the sample-end note, the Morrison disclosure, the gloss credits, the figure-term choice, our 14 glosses and the sense choices (tables above). `Modern English: James E. Morrison.` now reads `Modern rendering, folded under each section: James E. Morrison.` (hero) and `Modern rendering: James E. Morrison.` (closing credit).")
out.append("- Whole-treatise pass: star names corrected: `Aldeboran` → `Aldeberan` (Chaucer's spelling), `Alhaioth` → `Alhajoth` (attested form). Star-name rows marked verified (Skeat notes / Wikipedia). New entries: contents group titles and subtitles, `P`, the full-list disclosure, the `· supplementary` / `· spurious` kicker suffixes, the inline sword window's legend and label, the \"HERE ENDETH\" rubric, Skeat's group labels and colophon (source text), and the in-scene labels. The \"Modern rendering — pending\" note now appears on 11 sections.")
out.append("- Contents: the collapsible full list (`Every section, by its first words`, and its first-words entries such as `Thyn Astrolabie hath a ring…`) removed (Jes tg 17849). Navigation is the major-divisions row and the star lines under each part.")
out.append('- Star lines removed (Jes tg 17894, 17896): the star-link lines under each part heading and under the supplementary and spurious heads are gone, with their nav labels and star names; navigation is the major-divisions row at the top. Prologue (Jes tg 17901): every figure now sits at its own line, with a red `☞` before its phrase; the sword window moved from after the paragraph to `with this swerd`. New window: the languages map (tg 17891).')
out.append("- Gloss pass over the rest of Part I (§§ 4–23; Jes tg 17907): the glosses and the modern line now run from the Prologue through Part I § 23; new `ours` respellings, sense choices and line departures are in the tables above (all provisional). The sample-end note moved after § 23 and now reads `The glosses run through Part I.` / `Part II is shown in Skeat's text without glosses, for now.`; the credit line says `for the Prologue and Part I`. Skeat's _italic_ Latin now renders in italics on both lines. Bare numerals (90, 31, 23) now sit in the line too, the numeral repeated beneath (no new wording). Written from the Middle English, Skeat's glossaries and notes and plain English only; no modern translation was consulted.")
out.append("")
